// Standard Capability Interface: Admission
//
// A host admits some things only under a rule its people set: a secret that
// asks first, an action that needs a second approval. The rule is an
// admission policy, a pure function from what is about to be admitted to
// `Allow`, `Deny(why)` or `AlsoAsk(participant)` (spec §10.1). This interface
// is what a host hands such a policy. Hosts fill it without putting any app
// names or business words into the interface: what kind of thing it is, is
// data.

// The program request the asker is working on now: the host's name for the
// program, and a digest of the program's current text. A policy that compares
// the digest admits the program only while its text is the one somebody read.
type work = { program: string, digest: string }

// What a host is about to admit.
type request = {
  // The kind of thing, in the host's words, as in "secret.use".
  what: string,
  // What it is done to.
  target: string,
  // Where it is asked from.
  place: string,
  // Whose authority the asker runs under.
  owner: string,
  // None when the asker is working on no program's request.
  work: option<work>,
}
